  "name": "FurCalvaDance",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurCalvaDance is an annual furry convention organized by NormandiFurs in Saint Martin des Entrées, Calvados, France. The first edition, in January 2019, was the first large furmeet in Normandy, and its success inspired a recurring annual furry dance event. Programming includes fursuit-optional competitive games, FurOctaGone dance battles, video and board games, a dealers' den, tabletop gaming and nightly dances with DJs, and a complimentary brunch comes with basic registration. In 2025 the event moved to the vacation village Le Sénéquet, and attendance has grown from 49 to 219.",
